Foxwarm build patch for the Monty standalone worker (pydantic/monty v1.6.0, MIT License; see
MONTY-LICENSE). It replaces the ty-based type checker (crate monty-type-checking, with ruff, ty,
salsa and the embedded typeshed) by a stub of the same API, so the `monty` executable links none of
it. Foxwarm starts `monty subprocess` and never asks for type checking, so the checker is
unreachable there; a request for type checking reports that type checking is not available. The
interpreter and the worker protocol are unchanged. The crate's other source files stay in the
tree, unreferenced.
Applied by scripts/release/native-source.py (git apply) before scripts/release/build-monty.sh builds.

